        {
            "_id": "FghL14nU7EtFGROX",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
            "name": "Unstable Magic",
            "sort": 800000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A roiling incant is as much a mass of unstable magic as it is a creature. Is isn't living or undead, nor is it even a construct. It can't be healed or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Repair]{Repaired} and is destroyed at 0 Hit Points, though it naturally recovers a number of Hit Points equal to its @Damage[(@actor.level*@actor.system.abilities.con.mod)[healing]]{level × its Constitution modifier} each day.</p>\n<p>Each time a roiling incant casts one of its non-cantrip spells, it drains its own magic to do so, taking @Damage[5[force]] damage.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": []
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        }
